best = inject_before_faq(best, '''<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Pick Broken Scissors when you can maintain close-range hits and protect Sharpness uptime.</li><li>Pick Magic Scissors + Fireball when you can create space, aim and charge safely.</li><li>Treat named Imprints and Relics as priorities, not guaranteed drops.</li><li>Use real-time DPS with the same encounter and one changed component.</li><li>Judge clear time and damage taken alongside the DPS number.</li></ul></section><h2 id="loadouts">Complete loadout plans</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>Broken route</th><th>Magic route</th><th>If the piece does not appear</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Scissors</td><td>Broken Scissors</td><td>Magic Scissors</td><td>Keep the chosen weapon; do not rebuild the run around a random reward</td></tr><tr><td>Spell</td><td>A fast option that can cover lost contact</td><td>Fireball</td><td>Choose a Spell that preserves range and charge timing</td></tr><tr><td>Special Skill</td><td>Rush</td><td>A movement or spacing tool</td><td>Keep one reliable engage or escape action</td></tr><tr><td>Weapon Imprint</td><td>Hunger for maintained uptime; Frenzy for conversion into speed</td><td>Threading for repeated hits; Downpour for a different projectile pattern</td><td>Select the branch that preserves the same input rhythm</td></tr><tr><td>Relic bridge</td><td>Cat's Eye Ring</td><td>Blue Chakram</td><td>Take uptime, control or recovery rather than an unrelated trigger</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="fallbacks">Random-reward fallback rules</h2><p>A best-build page should survive the roguelike reward system. The priority list is not a promise that every named piece appears. When a preferred Imprint or Relic is absent, keep the primary action intact. Broken Scissors still needs repeated hits and a way back into range; Magic Scissors still needs safe charging and a useful release line. Replace the missing piece by function, not by name.</p><ol><li>Keep the selected Scissors and its input cadence.</li><li>Protect the weakest moment: reconnecting for melee or creating space for charge.</li><li>Prefer a reward that improves an action already present in the loop.</li><li>Avoid a conditional bonus whose trigger the loadout cannot produce.</li><li>Re-evaluate only after the next comparable encounter.</li></ol><h2 id="dps">DPS comparison method</h2><p>Version 1.0 adds a real-time DPS display, but a single peak number does not prove a build. Use the same chapter, encounter type and difficulty. Keep the Scissors, Spell and Special Skill fixed. Change one Imprint or Relic, then record the sustained DPS window, clear time and damage taken. Repeat at least once because enemy movement and random rewards can distort one attempt.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Measurement</th><th>What it answers</th><th>Bad comparison</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sustained DPS</td><td>Does the loop keep producing damage?</td><td>Comparing a boss to a crowd of small enemies</td></tr><tr><td>Clear time</td><td>Does setup time erase the damage gain?</td><td>Changing chapter and loadout together</td></tr><tr><td>Damage taken</td><td>Can the player execute the loop safely?</td><td>Ignoring failed charge or combo attempts</td></tr><tr><td>Uptime</td><td>How often is Sharpness or charge ready?</td><td>Reporting only one ideal burst</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="failures">Failure symptoms and corrections</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause to test</th><th>Correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Broken route never reaches its crit window</td><td>Too many gaps between hits</td><td>Use Rush to reconnect and prefer the branch that tolerates your real uptime</td></tr><tr><td>Sharpness reaches full but output remains inconsistent</td><td>Crit window begins while targets are leaving range</td><td>Build the resource on a cluster and preserve movement for the window</td></tr><tr><td>Magic route takes damage during charge</td><td>Charging before establishing space</td><td>Move first, align the lane, then charge</td></tr><tr><td>Fireball consumes setup on a weak target</td><td>Weapon-to-Spell handoff is mistimed</td><td>Confirm the intended crit/resource state before casting</td></tr><tr><td>DPS rises but clears get worse</td><td>Setup or survival cost exceeds the gain</td><td>Use clear time and damage taken as the deciding measures</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="verification">Current-tooltip verification</h2><p>Open the current 1.0 tooltip for each named Imprint and Relic. Confirm the trigger, affected skill, duration and any cap. The official previews establish the interaction direction, but Team Tapas warned that detailed effects and values could change. If the live tooltip differs, follow it and treat this guide's old wording as a correction candidate.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Team Tapas 1.0 notes and previews</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Evidence states and media hashes</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Related pages</h2><a href="broken-scissors-sharpness-build.html">Broken Scissors full guide</a><a href="magic-scissors-fireball-build.html">Magic Scissors full guide</a><a href="../guides/weapons.html">Compare all five Scissors</a><a href="../guides/armory.html">Prepare the Armory</a></div>''')

broken = inject_before_faq(broken, '''<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><p>Build Sharpness through real hits, use Rush to restore contact, and use Cat's Eye Ring as a Spell-to-Sharpness bridge if the live tooltip still matches the preview. Choose Hunger only when the run can maintain its condition; choose Frenzy when converting current Sharpness into faster output better fits your execution.</p></section><h2 id="components">Component jobs</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Job in the loop</th><th>Verify in 1.0</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Broken Scissors</td><td>Gain Sharpness from hits; reach the crit state</td><td>Sharpness trigger and full-gauge effect</td></tr><tr><td>Rush</td><td>Reconnect, thread targets and support close-range uptime</td><td>Current recast and pull wording</td></tr><tr><td>Hunger</td><td>Reward a run that continually gains Sharpness</td><td>Ceiling and failure condition</td></tr><tr><td>Frenzy</td><td>Convert Sharpness into attack-speed pressure</td><td>Conversion rule and cap</td></tr><tr><td>Cat's Eye Ring</td><td>Link Spell use back to Sharpness</td><td>Trigger, amount and cooldown</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="branches">Two practical branches</h2><h3>Uptime branch: Hunger</h3><p>Take this direction when the room layout, movement skill and target behavior allow frequent hits. Enter a cluster with Rush available, build Sharpness without long empty swings and avoid spending the crit window while enemies are scattering. If the previewed loss condition repeatedly triggers, the theoretical ceiling is not helping the actual run.</p><h3>Conversion branch: Frenzy</h3><p>Use this direction when the build reaches Sharpness reliably and benefits more from faster attack output. Faster actions do not remove the need to choose safe contact. Treat the branch as a way to capitalize on the resource, not permission to stand inside every attack.</p><h2 id="fallback">Fallback when the named reward is missing</h2><p>Keep three functions: approach, uptime and survival. A movement option can replace some of Rush's positioning value; a fast Spell can preserve a Spell-use trigger; a control or recovery reward can protect the time needed to rebuild Sharpness. Avoid taking a bonus that only activates at range if the weapon still requires close contact.</p><ol><li>Confirm the weapon can land repeated hits in the current room.</li><li>Save movement for the moment contact breaks.</li><li>Use the Spell only when it also solves positioning, control or a confirmed Relic trigger.</li><li>At full Sharpness, attack a stable target instead of chasing a nearly defeated one.</li><li>Reset before greed turns the crit window into lost health.</li></ol><h2 id="broken-fixes">When the build fails</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely reason</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sharpness stays low</td><td>Attacks miss or contact breaks</td><td>Shorten the approach and use Rush later</td></tr><tr><td>Sharpness collapses during movement</td><td>The chosen branch demands more uptime than the room allows</td><td>Switch away from the fragile condition</td></tr><tr><td>Full gauge produces little value</td><td>No target remains inside the weapon's effective range</td><td>Build against a cluster or durable target</td></tr><tr><td>Spells interrupt melee rhythm</td><td>Casting without a positioning purpose</td><td>Use the Spell during forced disengagement</td></tr><tr><td>Damage is high but runs fail</td><td>Survival cost is ignored</td><td>Trade one damage reward for control or recovery</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="broken-test">Tooltip and DPS check</h2><p>Read the current trigger and duration for every previewed piece. Then compare the same encounter with Hunger and Frenzy while holding the rest of the loadout fixed. Record time at full Sharpness, sustained DPS, clear time and damage taken. A branch wins only if the player can execute it repeatedly.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Team Tapas announcements</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Evidence and correction rules</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Related guides</h2><a href="garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Compare both build routes</a><a href="magic-scissors-fireball-build.html">Ranged alternative</a><a href="../guides/controls.html">Controls for combo play</a></div>''')

magic = inject_before_faq(magic, '''<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><p>Create space, line up the piercing release, cross the first Magic Scissors charge gauge, and use the resulting critical-hit interaction with Blue Chakram only if the current tooltip confirms it. Fireball is the documented charged Spell partner; Threading/Downpour and Rapid Fire/Fragment are separate branches, not a requirement to collect every name.</p></section><h2 id="magic-components">Component jobs</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Job</th><th>Live check</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Magic Scissors</td><td>Charged piercing projectile and crit setup</td><td>Gauge threshold and projectile behavior</td></tr><tr><td>Fireball</td><td>Charged Spell payoff and burning effect</td><td>Charge stages and current burn wording</td></tr><tr><td>Threading</td><td>Repeated tracking hits in the preview</td><td>Damage tradeoff and tracking count</td></tr><tr><td>Downpour</td><td>Different projectile output at a capped charge</td><td>Charge cap and extra projectile condition</td></tr><tr><td>Rapid Fire / Fragment</td><td>Multi-projectile or post-explosion Fireball branches</td><td>Projectile count, trigger and damage changes</td></tr><tr><td>Blue Chakram</td><td>Bridge weapon crits into Spell Rampage</td><td>Resource trigger, duration and consumption</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="magic-branches">Two branch patterns</h2><h3>Repeated-hit pattern</h3><p>Threading and Rapid Fire point toward more individual hits. This direction makes sense only if the current effects preserve enough damage and the encounter gives tracking projectiles valid targets. Use it when moving enemies or on-hit conditions matter more than one concentrated release.</p><h3>Projectile-volume pattern</h3><p>Downpour and Fragment point toward more projectiles around a practical charge and explosion. Create a clear lane before holding the input. More projectiles do not help if the player releases into terrain, a finished target or a room that forces constant interruption.</p><h2 id="magic-loop">Execution loop</h2><ol><li>Move until the nearest threat cannot immediately interrupt a held input.</li><li>Align multiple enemies so piercing can create real value.</li><li>Charge Magic Scissors past the confirmed threshold and release.</li><li>Check the crit or resource state instead of assuming it occurred.</li><li>Charge and cast Fireball at a target that justifies spending the setup.</li><li>Reposition before beginning the next charge.</li></ol><h2 id="magic-fallback">Fallback rules</h2><p>If Blue Chakram does not appear, Magic Scissors remains a ranged charge weapon; select control, charge safety or direct weapon support rather than a Relic with an unusable trigger. If Fireball's preferred branch is missing, keep the base charged behavior and choose a reward that preserves aim and release timing. The run should still function without a perfect screenshot loadout.</p><h2 id="magic-fixes">Failure symptoms</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause to test</th><th>Correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Charge is interrupted</td><td>Started too close to an active enemy</td><td>Create space before holding the input</td></tr><tr><td>Projectiles hit only one weak target</td><td>Release line ignores piercing</td><td>Move sideways until enemies overlap</td></tr><tr><td>Blue Chakram does not feed Fireball</td><td>Crit threshold, trigger or current tooltip differs</td><td>Verify the live effect and confirm the resource indicator</td></tr><tr><td>Fireball lands after enemies move</td><td>Charging without control or prediction</td><td>Cast on a stable cluster or shorten the charge</td></tr><tr><td>Peak DPS is high but survival is poor</td><td>Too much stationary setup</td><td>Prefer a mobility or control fallback</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="magic-test">Controlled comparison</h2><p>Keep the same chapter and loadout, then compare one branch at a time. Measure sustained DPS, hit rate, time spent charging, clear time and damage taken. The current in-game tooltip determines detailed effects because Team Tapas marked preview values as changeable.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Team Tapas announcements</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Evidence labels and media ledger</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Related guides</h2><a href="garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Compare build routes</a><a href="broken-scissors-sharpness-build.html">Melee alternative</a><a href="../guides/controls.html">Mouse aim and control modes</a></div>''')

weapons = inject_before_faq(weapons, '''<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><p>Choose Scissors by input rhythm before chasing a ranking: full combo for Scissors and Giant Scissors, aim-and-charge for Magic Scissors, repeated contact for Broken Scissors. Singing Scissors is confirmed as a current weapon, but this guide leaves its detailed mechanic to the live tooltip until a primary-source capture exists.</p></section><h2 id="profiles">All five Scissors profiles</h2><h3>Scissors: balanced full-combo baseline</h3><p>The default route teaches the version 1.0 combo rule: finishing the complete chain produces its unique attack. Use it to learn when an enemy opening lasts long enough for the finisher. Pair it with a Spell or Special Skill that creates that opening rather than one that asks you to abandon the chain.</p><h3>Giant Scissors: deliberate combo commitment</h3><p>Official notes place Giant Scissors in the full-combo family. Treat it as a commitment test: if the player repeatedly leaves before the unique ending attack, the weapon's defining condition is not being used. Prioritize space, control and a safe finishing window.</p><h3>Magic Scissors: charged piercing range</h3><p>Magic Scissors asks the player to aim, hold and release. Official material confirms piercing projectiles and the critical behavior after the first charge gauge. It fits a player who can create distance and line up more than one target. Pairing direction should protect charge time or reward the confirmed critical release.</p><h3>Broken Scissors: Sharpness from contact</h3><p>Broken Scissors gains Sharpness when attacks hit, and the official preview says full Sharpness makes attacks critical. It fits continuous close-range pressure. Choose movement, control and Spell interactions that help maintain contact rather than bonuses that only work while disengaged.</p><h3>Singing Scissors: verify before publishing a mechanic</h3><p>Singing Scissors is one of the five named routes. This page does not repeat another site's attack-speed or special-mechanic claims without official or reproducible 1.0 evidence. Open the unlocked weapon in the Armory, capture its current tooltip and use that wording as the starting point.</p><h2 id="unlock-boundary">Unlock boundary</h2><p>A new save begins with the default Scissors and limited Spells. Additional Scissors and Spells unlock through chapter progress and other conditions. The official material does not establish every exact unlock condition used by this page, so the correct action is to clear progress, return to Sil's House and check the Armory rather than follow an invented chapter table.</p><h2 id="wrong-choice">Wrong weapon symptoms</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>What happens</th><th>Mismatch</th><th>Try instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Combo finisher rarely appears</td><td>The player cannot hold the full chain safely</td><td>Create space with another skill or choose a shorter-feeling rhythm</td></tr><tr><td>Charged shots are constantly interrupted</td><td>Magic Scissors selected without spacing</td><td>Add movement/control or use a contact-based weapon</td></tr><tr><td>Sharpness never stabilizes</td><td>Broken Scissors selected while frequently disengaging</td><td>Use Rush/repositioning better or return to a combo route</td></tr><tr><td>Weapon feels strong only in one room type</td><td>The supporting Spell does not cover its weak matchup</td><td>Change the Spell, not every slot</td></tr><tr><td>A guide promises an unsupported Singing mechanic</td><td>No primary evidence</td><td>Read the current Armory tooltip and capture the version</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="weapon-test">How to compare weapons</h2><ol><li>Use the same chapter and difficulty.</li><li>Keep Spells and the Special Skill fixed where possible.</li><li>Run each Scissors long enough to perform its defining input correctly.</li><li>Record sustained DPS, clear time, interruptions and damage taken.</li><li>Choose the route with repeatable execution, not the largest isolated hit.</li></ol><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources and boundary</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official 1.0 launch notes and previews</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Evidence labels and correction format</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Build and loadout guides</h2><a href="../builds/broken-scissors-sharpness-build.html">Broken Scissors profile build</a><a href="../builds/magic-scissors-fireball-build.html">Magic Scissors profile build</a><a href="armory.html">Armory unlocks and loadouts</a></div>''')

changes = inject_before_faq(changes, '''<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><p>If a guide tells you to stack Attribute, Synergy or Rune systems, it targets an obsolete build. Version 1.0 moves decisions into skill-specific inputs, Level 3 Imprints, Relic connections, Armory loadouts, expanded Epilogues and post-Epilogue 3 Challenge Mode.</p></section><h2 id="migration">Early Access to 1.0 migration</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Old expectation</th><th>1.0 question</th><th>Player action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Global Attribute stack</td><td>Which skill-specific action produces damage?</td><td>Learn the Scissors combo, charge or resource loop</td></tr><tr><td>Synergy tags</td><td>Which two equipped pieces directly interact?</td><td>Read triggers on Imprints and Relics</td></tr><tr><td>Rune slot</td><td>Which current upgrade branch changes behavior?</td><td>Inspect the Level 3 Imprint choices</td></tr><tr><td>Old story ending</td><td>Has the save cleared all three Epilogues?</td><td>Continue through Epilogue 3</td></tr><tr><td>No mouse aiming</td><td>Which control scheme matches this build?</td><td>Use Keyboard &amp; Mouse, Keyboard-Only or Gamepad</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="update-checklist">Returning-player checklist</h2><ol><li>Open settings and select the intended control scheme.</li><li>Visit the Armory and rebuild the loadout with current Scissors, Spells and Special Skill.</li><li>Read every current tooltip instead of translating an old Rune recipe.</li><li>Push one skill toward its Imprint branch and connect skills through a relevant Relic.</li><li>Use real-time DPS for a same-encounter comparison.</li><li>Complete Epilogues 1–3 before looking for Challenge Mode.</li></ol><h2 id="update-fixes">Common update confusion</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Reason</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Old build cannot be recreated</td><td>Its systems were removed</td><td>Identify the desired action and rebuild it with current components</td></tr><tr><td>A named preview value differs</td><td>Pre-launch details were subject to change</td><td>Use the live 1.0 tooltip</td></tr><tr><td>Mouse controls seem absent</td><td>Wrong control scheme selected</td><td>Choose Keyboard &amp; Mouse in settings</td></tr><tr><td>Challenge Mode is missing</td><td>Epilogue 3 not cleared on this save</td><td>Complete and continue the correct save</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Team Tapas official 1.0 notes</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Evidence labels</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Use the new systems</h2><a href="armory.html">Armory loadouts</a><a href="controls.html">Control schemes</a><a href="challenge-mode.html">Challenge Mode</a><a href="../builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Current build routes</a></div>''')

armory = inject_before_faq(armory, '''<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><p>Use the Armory before a run to equip unlocked Scissors, Spells and a Special Skill. Keep one primary damage rhythm, one answer to its unsafe moment and one fallback plan for random in-run rewards.</p></section><h2 id="slots">Loadout slot jobs</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>Decision</th><th>Bad sign</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Scissors</td><td>Choose combo, charge or repeated-contact rhythm</td><td>You cannot execute its defining input</td></tr><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Add range, control, burst or a confirmed resource bridge</td><td>It competes with the weapon without covering a weakness</td></tr><tr><td>Special Skill</td><td>Give it one job: engage, escape, setup or burst</td><td>It is always unavailable when the weapon becomes unsafe</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="unlock-fix">Missing unlock checklist</h2><ol><li>Confirm the intended chapter or Epilogue was cleared on this save.</li><li>Return to Sil's House instead of beginning another run immediately.</li><li>Open the Armory and inspect every category.</li><li>Read the current tooltip and compare the item against the equipped baseline.</li><li>If absent, continue official story progress; do not rely on an unsourced exact unlock table.</li></ol><h2 id="armory-fixes">Loadout troubleshooting</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New weapon feels weaker</td><td>Its combo or charge condition is not being completed</td><td>Practice its defining input before comparing DPS</td></tr><tr><td>All four skills need different setups</td><td>No single damage engine</td><td>Rebuild around one repeatable action</td></tr><tr><td>Unlocked option does not appear</td><td>Wrong save or progress state</td><td>Continue the latest cleared save and recheck</td></tr><tr><td>Run depends on one rare reward</td><td>No fallback</td><td>Choose a functional substitute for uptime, control or recovery</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official 1.0 notes</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Evidence boundary</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Related guides</h2><a href="weapons.html">Compare Scissors</a><a href="../builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Plan a build</a><a href="../walkthrough.html">Story checkpoints</a></div>''')

controls = inject_before_faq(controls, '''<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><p>Use Keyboard &amp; Mouse for free aiming and mouse-button actions, Keyboard-Only for a familiar directional rhythm, or Gamepad if controller movement is more consistent. Test the chosen scheme with the actual build input before a long run.</p></section><h2 id="setup-controls">Five-minute setup</h2><ol><li>Choose the control scheme in settings.</li><li>Test movement and the full Scissors combo.</li><li>Hold and release one charged action.</li><li>Activate the Spell and Special Skill while moving.</li><li>Open a menu and confirm navigation works.</li></ol><h2 id="control-fixes">Input troubleshooting</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Check</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Magic Scissors releases in the wrong direction</td><td>Control scheme and cursor position</td><td>Use Keyboard &amp; Mouse and aim before charging</td></tr><tr><td>Combo stops while moving</td><td>Conflicting or uncomfortable bindings</td><td>Rebind the action or choose the more stable scheme</td></tr><tr><td>Menu ignores expected input</td><td>Active scheme and focus</td><td>Use the supported mouse menu control or selected gamepad</td></tr><tr><td>Old key map does not match</td><td>Guide version or localization</td><td>Follow the live settings screen</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="control-boundary">Version boundary</h2><p class="source-note">Official 1.0 notes confirm Keyboard &amp; Mouse as the default, free mouse aiming, mouse-button assignments and continued Keyboard-Only support. Exact key labels can vary, so the current settings screen is authoritative.</p><div class="related-reading"><h2>Match controls to a build</h2><a href="../builds/magic-scissors-fireball-build.html">Ranged charge route</a><a href="../builds/broken-scissors-sharpness-build.html">Close-range Sharpness route</a><a href="getting-started.html">First-run setup</a></div>''')

# Long-form additions keep each page useful beyond a metadata rewrite. They avoid
# unsupported balance numbers and turn every recommendation into a reproducible check.
best = inject_before_faq(best, '''<h2 id="run-plan">Run plan from Armory to result</h2><p>Before leaving Sil's House, write the build in four jobs rather than four names: primary damage, safe approach, payoff and fallback. For Broken Scissors, the weapon owns primary damage, Rush handles approach and the crit window is the payoff. For Magic Scissors, the charged weapon creates the setup, movement creates time and Fireball spends the payoff. This job map makes random rewards easier to judge.</p><p>During early rooms, do not measure a route by how many colored upgrades it has. Ask whether the next reward makes the core input more available or more reliable. A reward that adds damage only after an unused trigger is weaker than a modest reward that lets the player finish another combo, hold another charge or stay inside Sharpness range.</p><h3>Before a boss or durable target</h3><ul><li>Enter with the movement action available instead of spending it on a nearly defeated enemy.</li><li>Know which visible state proves the engine is ready: full Sharpness, a completed charge threshold or the confirmed resource indicator.</li><li>Keep one exit path. Peak DPS is not useful when the entire setup ends in avoidable damage.</li><li>Use the first safe cycle as a measurement. If the setup fails, change timing before blaming the component list.</li></ul><h2 id="best-scenarios">Which route fits the current problem?</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Player problem</th><th>Better first test</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Enemies spread across the room</td><td>Magic Scissors</td><td>Piercing lines reward deliberate alignment</td></tr><tr><td>Durable target allows constant contact</td><td>Broken Scissors</td><td>Repeated hits can build and use Sharpness</td></tr><tr><td>The player panics while holding charge</td><td>Broken or default combo route</td><td>A charge build cannot win if the input is abandoned</td></tr><tr><td>The player greedily stays in melee</td><td>Magic route or a safer Broken fallback</td><td>Distance can expose timing mistakes more clearly</td></tr><tr><td>Random rewards split the plan</td><td>Keep the current weapon and choose by function</td><td>A coherent imperfect route beats four unrelated conditions</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>No table proves a universal tier list. It identifies the next controlled test. A route becomes the better build for a player when its defining action survives real room pressure and produces repeatable clears.</p>''')
broken = inject_before_faq(broken, '''<h2 id="sharpness-management">Managing the Sharpness window</h2><p>Think in three phases: build, convert and exit. During the build phase, land reliable attacks rather than swinging at empty space. During conversion, spend the full-gauge crit state on a cluster or durable target. During exit, leave before enemy pressure turns the window into a trade. The next approach begins only when movement and target position support another cycle.</p><p>Rush belongs at the transition between phases. Using it too early can leave no approach tool when contact breaks. Using it only as panic movement can waste its offensive setup. The useful timing is the point where its confirmed movement and thread behavior restores a real attack opportunity.</p><h3>Room-type adjustments</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Room state</th><th>Sharpness plan</th><th>What to avoid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Many small enemies</td><td>Build on a stable edge of the group and convert into nearby targets</td><td>Chasing one low-health enemy across the room</td></tr><tr><td>One durable enemy</td><td>Use safe openings to build and reserve movement for forced disengagement</td><td>Assuming constant contact is always safe</td></tr><tr><td>Fast moving targets</td><td>Prioritize approach and control rewards</td><td>Selecting a fragile uptime condition without a reconnect plan</td></tr><tr><td>Heavy incoming pressure</td><td>Use shorter cycles and accept partial resource</td><td>Standing still merely to preserve a theoretical maximum</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="broken-record">Record a reproducible result</h2><p>A useful player-tested claim needs the game version, chapter, difficulty, Scissors, Spell, Special Skill, Imprint, Relic and changed component. Capture the tooltip and an uncut combat window. Report sustained behavior, not only the frame where Sharpness is full. This distinguishes a strong interaction from a lucky room.</p><p>If the result contradicts the preview, do not force the old description. Mark the current 1.0 tooltip as the active state, retain the preview as historical context and update the trigger or effect. That makes the guide correctable instead of pretending launch balance never changed.</p>''')
magic = inject_before_faq(magic, '''<h2 id="charge-management">Charge management by encounter</h2><p>A charge is a commitment with an opportunity cost. The player gives up immediate movement or output to create a stronger release. That trade is favorable only when distance, enemy recovery or control produces enough time. Begin by reading the room, not by holding the button automatically.</p><p>Piercing changes target selection. The nearest enemy is not always the best aim point. A short sideways movement can align several bodies and turn one release into multiple useful hits. If alignment takes too long, release earlier or reposition; an interrupted maximum charge produces less value than a safe partial cycle.</p><h3>Fireball handoff decisions</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>State after Magic Scissors</th><th>Fireball decision</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Confirmed crit/resource and stable cluster</td><td>Begin the intended charged payoff</td><td>The setup and target both exist</td></tr><tr><td>Resource unclear</td><td>Check the indicator or tooltip behavior first</td><td>Do not spend from an assumed state</td></tr><tr><td>Enemies are about to leave the area</td><td>Shorten or delay the charge</td><td>A missed maximum release has no value</td></tr><tr><td>Threat is entering melee range</td><td>Move or use control</td><td>Survival protects the next cycle</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="magic-record">What a valid test captures</h2><p>Record the exact Magic Scissors and Fireball tooltips, the selected branches, Blue Chakram wording, chapter and difficulty. For the combat sample, preserve the full sequence from spacing to weapon release to Spell cast. The DPS display should be visible, but also record misses, interrupted charges, clear time and damage taken.</p><p>Compare Threading and Downpour separately, then compare Rapid Fire and Fragment separately. Changing both weapon and Spell branches at once prevents attribution. If a branch increases hit count but lowers practical clear speed, describe that result instead of calling the larger visual effect stronger.</p>''')
weapons = inject_before_faq(weapons, '''<h2 id="pairing-directions">Pairing direction by weakness</h2><p>A weapon guide should not prescribe one Spell for every run. Pair by the moment where the Scissors stops working. Full-combo routes need time and control for the finisher. Magic Scissors needs space and a release line. Broken Scissors needs approach and continued contact. The supporting slot should solve that weakness or connect through a confirmed trigger.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Scissors family</th><th>Weak moment</th><th>Useful support direction</th><th>Misleading choice</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Full combo</td><td>Enemy interrupts before the ending attack</td><td>Control, spacing or a safe engage</td><td>Another long commitment with no protection</td></tr><tr><td>Charged projectile</td><td>Threat reaches Sil during charge</td><td>Movement, control or shorter practical setup</td><td>A bonus that assumes every release reaches maximum charge</td></tr><tr><td>Sharpness contact</td><td>Target leaves melee range</td><td>Reconnect, pull or resource-preserving interaction</td><td>A distant condition that never helps regain contact</td></tr><tr><td>Unverified Singing route</td><td>Mechanic not established here</td><td>Read and capture the live tooltip first</td><td>Copying an unsupported number or cadence</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="unlock-capture">How to document an unlock</h2><p>When a new Scissors appears, record the current save progress, the last completed chapter or Epilogue, the Armory screen and the full tooltip. One isolated unlock does not prove the only condition, so phrase the result carefully: the weapon was available after that state, not necessarily because of an invented single trigger.</p><p>For Singing Scissors, a useful capture includes the weapon name, full mechanic text, version number and an uncut demonstration of its defining input. Until that exists, this page preserves an explicit unknown. That is more useful to search engines and players than a confident paragraph built from another site's claim.</p><h2 id="selection-workflow">Five-step selection workflow</h2><ol><li>Choose the input rhythm that feels executable.</li><li>Perform the defining action against a stable target.</li><li>Identify the moment the weapon becomes unsafe or stops producing value.</li><li>Use Spell and Special Skill slots to cover that moment.</li><li>Compare the result with the same encounter, not a different chapter.</li></ol><p>Revisit the choice after new Armory unlocks, but change only one slot during the comparison. A new weapon may initially feel weak because its charge, combo or resource condition has not been learned.</p>''')
home += '''<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">How to use this wiki</p><h2>Start with the symptom, then verify the current tooltip.</h2></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Player symptom</th><th>First page</th><th>Decision after reading</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Damage falls off during a run</td><td><a href="builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Best Build</a></td><td>Choose one core loop and one fallback</td></tr><tr><td>A weapon feels awkward</td><td><a href="guides/weapons.html">Weapons</a></td><td>Match input rhythm to the player</td></tr><tr><td>An unlock is missing</td><td><a href="guides/armory.html">Armory</a></td><td>Verify progress, save and current category</td></tr><tr><td>The next story step is unclear</td><td><a href="walkthrough.html">Walkthrough</a></td><td>Check the eight-step 1.0 route</td></tr><tr><td>Endgame does not appear</td><td><a href="guides/challenge-mode.html">Challenge Mode</a></td><td>Continue the Epilogue 3-cleared save</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Every mechanics page uses the same correction rule. Official 1.0 notes establish the released system and progression state. Official previews can establish a named interaction, but detailed values remain provisional when the developer warned they could change. A current tooltip capture overrides a preview; a player-tested conclusion requires the version, loadout, chapter and repeatable comparison.</p><p>This boundary matters for GEO as much as player trust. Direct answers stay short enough to quote, fact tables keep entities and relationships explicit, and visible FAQs match structured data. Unknown mechanics remain unknown rather than becoming plausible-sounding filler.</p></section>'''
changes = inject_before_faq(changes, '''<h2 id="measure-change">Use the new DPS display without fooling yourself</h2><p>Keep chapter, encounter and core loadout fixed. Change one Imprint or Relic, then compare sustained output, clear time and damage taken. A higher peak can still be worse when the new input causes more interruption or setup time. Version 1.0 gives the measurement tool; the player still needs a controlled comparison.</p><h2 id="change-sources">Source boundary</h2><p>The launch notes are authoritative for removed systems, controls, story additions and Challenge Mode. Preview posts support named examples but not guaranteed final numbers. The live tooltip is authoritative for the installed 1.0 build.</p>''')
armory = inject_before_faq(armory, '''<h2 id="armory-workflow">A/B test a new unlock</h2><p>Save the old loadout, equip one new component and enter the same progression state. Perform the new component's defining input correctly before comparing it. Record sustained DPS, clear time, interruptions and damage taken. If the new piece fixes the intended weakness without breaking the primary loop, keep it; otherwise restore the baseline and test a different slot.</p><p>Do not confuse an unlock with an upgrade. A newly available Scissors can be a different rhythm rather than a larger number. The Armory is a choice surface, not a straight power ladder.</p><h2 id="armory-boundary">Version boundary</h2><p class="source-note">Official 1.0 notes confirm Armory selection, limited starting options and additional unlocks through progress and other conditions. This guide does not invent a complete chapter-by-chapter unlock table.</p>''')
controls = inject_before_faq(controls, '''<h2 id="build-inputs">Build-specific input rehearsal</h2><p>For a full-combo Scissors, move around one target and verify that directional input does not accidentally cancel the chain. For Broken Scissors, practice approaching, landing several hits and leaving without losing track of hazards. For Magic Scissors, place the cursor first, hold through the intended gauge and release while movement pressure increases.</p><p>Repeat each rehearsal with the Spell and Special Skill. The important question is whether the player can activate the supporting action at the exact moment the weapon becomes unsafe. A comfortable menu binding that fails during movement is not a good combat binding.</p><h2 id="accessibility">Consistency before speed</h2><p>Reduce simultaneous finger conflicts and prefer a layout the player can repeat. Gamepad, Keyboard-Only and Keyboard &amp; Mouse are supported choices, not skill rankings. If aiming is accurate but movement collapses, lower the complexity or change the scheme. If movement is stable but projectiles miss, use the free-aim option and rehearse cursor placement.</p><p>After changing bindings, test one complete room before starting a long progression attempt. Record the live labels if publishing a key map because language and platform presentation can differ.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Team Tapas 1.0 notes</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Site source policy</a></li></ul></div>''')

getting_started_faq = [
    ("What should a new player do first in Garden of Witches?", "Choose a comfortable control scheme, learn the default Scissors full combo, and use one Spell to cover the moment when finishing that combo is unsafe."),
    ("What should I check after a failed run?", "Return to Sil's House, inspect the Armory for newly unlocked Scissors or Spells, and change only one loadout slot before the next attempt."),
    ("Should a beginner copy an Early Access build?", "No. Version 1.0 removed Attribute, Synergy and Rune systems. Use current Scissors, Spells, Imprints and Relics instead."),
]
getting_started = '''<header class="page-hero image-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Version 1.0 first-run route</p><h1>Garden of Witches Beginner Guide: First Run Tips</h1><p>Set controls, learn one repeatable attack loop, read room rewards, and check permanent progress after every return to Sil's House.</p></div><img src="../assets/media/steam-screenshot-01.jpg" width="600" height="338" alt="Sil fighting enemies in a Garden of Witches arena"></header><article class="article-layout"><div class="prose"><section class="direct-answer"><b>Direct answer</b><p>For a first run, use the default Scissors and finish its full combo only when enemies leave a safe opening. Pick a Spell or Special Skill that creates space when the combo becomes unsafe. After a run, return to the Armory, check for permanent unlocks, and change one slot at a time.</p></section>
<section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer checklist</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Use Keyboard &amp; Mouse for free aim, or keep Keyboard-Only if that movement pattern feels more reliable.</li><li>Learn one Scissors attack chain before judging damage.</li><li>Choose room rewards that improve the same repeatable action.</li><li>Do not force a high-risk room when health or recovery cannot support it.</li><li>Check the Armory after failure and after every chapter clear.</li></ul></section>
<h2 id="setup">1. Set controls before the first room</h2><p>Version 1.0 makes Keyboard &amp; Mouse the default and keeps Keyboard-Only and Gamepad available. Mouse aiming helps when a Spell or Scissors release travels in a chosen direction. Keyboard-Only can be easier for a returning Early Access player who already knows its movement rhythm. The right setup is the one that lets you move, aim and activate a defensive option without looking away from enemies.</p><p>Test movement, one basic combo, one Spell and one evasive action in a low-pressure space. If two actions compete for the same finger or a charged input cancels movement, change the binding before a real attempt. The live settings screen is the authority for key labels because localization and platform layouts can differ.</p>
<h2 id="loop">2. Build around one action loop</h2><div class="fact-grid"><article><b>Scissors</b><p>Your repeatable damage input and the rhythm that defines the run.</p></article><article><b>Spell</b><p>Covers the weapon's weak moment, adds range, control or burst.</p></article><article><b>Imprint</b><p>Changes how a particular skill behaves after its upgrade branch appears.</p></article><article><b>Relic</b><p>Connects separate skills or rewards a condition already present in the loop.</p></article></div><p>A coherent early build answers one question: what action can you repeat without taking unnecessary damage? The default Scissors rewards completing its attack chain, so learn when to finish and when to leave. Do not select three rewards that each ask for a different setup. One reliable interaction is more useful than several unrelated bonuses.</p>
<h2 id="rooms">3. Read room reward and risk</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Room decision</th><th>Take it when</th><th>Skip or choose safer when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Damage upgrade</td><td>It strengthens the attack you already land consistently</td><td>It only works during a condition you rarely create</td></tr><tr><td>New behavior / Imprint</td><td>The branch fixes range, timing or target coverage</td><td>It replaces a reliable loop with an unfamiliar one before a hard fight</td></tr><tr><td>Relic interaction</td><td>Both sides of the interaction are already in the loadout</td><td>It depends on a skill you do not have</td></tr><tr><td>Higher-risk route</td><td>Health, recovery and a boss-ready loop are stable</td><td>The last two rooms exposed the same failure</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Random rewards mean the exact planned loadout may not appear. Use a fallback rule: preserve the weapon's core rhythm, then replace the missing bonus with something that improves uptime, reach, control or recovery. Do not restart a coherent run only because one named preview item did not drop.</p>
<h2 id="armory">4. Use the Armory as a progress checkpoint</h2><ol><li>Return to Sil's House after a clear or failed attempt.</li><li>Open the Armory and look for newly available Scissors, Spells or Special Skills.</li><li>Read the current tooltip instead of relying on an Early Access description.</li><li>Equip one change and keep the remaining slots fixed.</li><li>Run the next chapter and note whether the changed slot solved the intended problem.</li></ol><p>Version 1.0 starts with the default Scissors and a limited Spell selection. More options unlock through chapter progress and other conditions. A failed combat attempt can still be useful when it reveals a permanent unlock or proves that the current loop fails at range, during recovery, or against groups.</p>
<h2 id="mistakes">Common beginner mistakes and fixes</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely mistake</th><th>Fix on the next attempt</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Damage feels low despite many upgrades</td><td>Rewards improve different actions</td><td>Choose one attack condition and make every new piece support it</td></tr><tr><td>Combo keeps getting interrupted</td><td>Starting the finisher without a safe opening</td><td>Use a Spell for space or leave before the final hit</td></tr><tr><td>Charged attacks miss</td><td>Charging before establishing direction and distance</td><td>Create space, aim, then hold and release</td></tr><tr><td>No new option appears</td><td>Wrong save state, uncompleted progress, or Armory not rechecked</td><td>Continue the latest cleared save and inspect the Armory after returning home</td></tr><tr><td>Old guide terms do not exist</td><td>The guide targets Early Access</td><td>Replace Attribute, Synergy and Rune advice with current 1.0 systems</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2 id="verify">Version and source boundary</h2><p class="source-note">Official 1.0 launch notes confirm the new control schemes, rebuilt Scissors/Spell/Imprint/Relic system and progression structure. Reward order and individual runs vary. Current tooltips decide exact effects; this page does not invent room probabilities or hidden unlock conditions.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Team Tapas official Steam news</a></li><li><a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/2530470/Garden_of_Witches/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Steam store and media</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Continue with a player task</h2><a href="weapons.html">Compare all five Scissors</a><a href="armory.html">Set the Armory loadout</a><a href="../builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Choose a documented build path</a><a href="../walkthrough.html">Follow the 1.0 story route</a></div>''' + faq_html(getting_started_faq) + '''</div><aside class="toc"><b>On this page</b><a href="#setup">Controls</a><a href="#loop">Build loop</a><a href="#rooms">Rooms and risk</a><a href="#armory">Armory check</a><a href="#mistakes">Mistakes</a><a href="#verify">Version boundary</a></aside></article>'''

wiki = '''<header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Player question index</p><h1>Garden of Witches Wiki</h1><p>Builds, Scissors, progression and controls for version 1.0.</p></header><section class="section"><div class="directory"><article><h2>Builds</h2><a href="builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Best build paths</a><a href="builds/broken-scissors-sharpness-build.html">Broken Scissors</a><a href="builds/magic-scissors-fireball-build.html">Magic Scissors + Fireball</a></article><article><h2>Systems</h2><a href="guides/weapons.html">All Scissors</a><a href="guides/armory.html">Armory</a><a href="guides/garden-of-witches-1-0-changes.html">1.0 changes</a></article><article><h2>Play</h2><a href="guides/getting-started.html">Beginner guide</a><a href="guides/controls.html">Controls</a><a href="walkthrough.html">Progression</a></article></div></section>'''
walkthrough_faq = [("How many chapters are in Garden of Witches 1.0?", "The official 1.0 route has five main chapters followed by Epilogues 1, 2 and 3."),("What should I do after each chapter?", "Return to Sil's House, inspect the Armory for new Scissors or Spells, read current tooltips and keep the cleared save."),("What unlocks after Epilogue 3?", "Challenge Mode unlocks. Continue the cleared save to enter the Challenge Mode version of Sil's House.")]
walkthrough = '''<header class="page-hero image-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Version 1.0 story route</p><h1>Garden of Witches Chapter Walkthrough: 1.0 Story Route</h1><p>Clear Chapters 1–5 and Epilogues 1–3, checking Sil's House and the Armory between clears before entering Challenge Mode.</p></div><img src="assets/media/steam-screenshot-04.jpg" width="600" height="338" alt="Sil speaking with Fiena during the Garden of Witches story"></header><article class="article-layout"><div class="prose"><section class="direct-answer"><b>Direct answer</b><p>Complete Chapters 1–5, then Epilogues 1–3 on the same progressing save. Check the Armory after every clear because new skills can unlock through progress. After Epilogue 3, continue that cleared save to reach the Challenge Mode version of Sil's House.</p></section><section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick route</h2><div class="progress-map"><span>Chapter 1</span><span>Chapter 2</span><span>Chapter 3</span><span>Chapter 4</span><span>Chapter 5</span><span>Epilogue 1</span><span>Epilogue 2</span><span>Epilogue 3</span><strong>Challenge Mode</strong></div></section>
<h2 id="route">Chapter-by-chapter preparation</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Route step</th><th>Player goal</th><th>Armory check after clear</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Chapter 1</td><td>Learn the default Scissors rhythm and preserve enough health to finish the route</td><td>Look for the first additional loadout options</td></tr><tr><td>Chapter 2</td><td>Confirm whether the Spell covers the weapon's unsafe moment</td><td>Compare any new option against one fixed baseline</td></tr><tr><td>Chapter 3</td><td>Build a coherent Imprint and Relic interaction rather than collecting unrelated power</td><td>Read every newly unlocked tooltip</td></tr><tr><td>Chapter 4</td><td>Prepare a loop that handles both groups and durable targets</td><td>Save the loadout that clears consistently</td></tr><tr><td>Chapter 5</td><td>Finish the main route without replacing a stable build immediately before the clear</td><td>Confirm the Epilogue route appears on the same save</td></tr><tr><td>Epilogue 1</td><td>Revalidate the build against post-story pressure</td><td>Check for permanent progress</td></tr><tr><td>Epilogue 2</td><td>Complete the route and inspect newly available skills</td><td>Official notes say new skills can unlock through later Epilogues</td></tr><tr><td>Epilogue 3</td><td>Clear the final 1.0 story step</td><td>Continue this cleared save for Challenge Mode</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2 id="between">Between chapters: five checks</h2><ol><li>Return to Sil's House and make sure the latest clear saved.</li><li>Open the Armory and inspect newly available Scissors, Spells and Special Skills.</li><li>Read the current 1.0 tooltip before equipping an unlock.</li><li>Change one loadout slot, not the whole build, when testing the new option.</li><li>Keep the previous reliable loadout in mind so a weak experiment does not block the route.</li></ol><p>The walkthrough does not assign unverified bosses, rooms or rewards to chapter numbers. The useful player need is the progression state: what to clear, what to inspect afterward and how to avoid continuing the wrong save.</p>
<h2 id="blocked">Progression not appearing: troubleshooting</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>What you see</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Next chapter or Epilogue does not appear</td><td>The clear did not complete or the game opened an earlier save</td><td>Return to the title screen, select the most recent progressing save and verify the last clear</td></tr><tr><td>Expected Scissors or Spell is absent</td><td>The unlock condition is not complete or the Armory has not been rechecked</td><td>Continue chapter progress, return home and inspect the Armory again</td></tr><tr><td>Challenge Mode is missing</td><td>Epilogue 3 is not cleared on this save</td><td>Finish Epilogue 3, keep that save and choose Continue</td></tr><tr><td>Sil's House looks unchanged after the clear</td><td>Wrong save or normal story state loaded</td><td>Exit and continue the exact Epilogue 3-cleared save</td></tr><tr><td>An old guide describes a different route</td><td>It targets Early Access</td><td>Use the five chapters plus three Epilogues structure from the 1.0 notes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2 id="challenge">After Epilogue 3</h2><p>Challenge Mode is not a shortcut for unfinished story progress. The official sequence is: clear Epilogue 3, continue the cleared save, arrive in Challenge Mode Sil's House, prepare the build, then leave through the door. Use the dedicated <a href="guides/challenge-mode.html">Challenge Mode guide</a> if the mode or entrance does not appear.</p><h2 id="sources">Version and source boundary</h2><p class="source-note">Team Tapas' official 1.0 notes confirm five main chapters, Epilogues 1–3, later skill unlocks and the Challenge Mode transition. Room sequences and run rewards remain variable; this route does not present guessed encounter details as fact.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Team Tapas Steam news</a></li><li><a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/2530470/Garden_of_Witches/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Garden of Witches Steam page</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Related guides</h2><a href="guides/armory.html">Armory unlocks and loadouts</a><a href="guides/challenge-mode.html">Unlock and enter Challenge Mode</a><a href="builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Prepare a version 1.0 build</a></div>''' + faq_html(walkthrough_faq) + '''</div><aside class="toc"><b>On this page</b><a href="#route">Chapters 1–5</a><a href="#between">Between clears</a><a href="#blocked">Troubleshooting</a><a href="#challenge">After Epilogue 3</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></aside></article>'''

challenge_faq = [("How do I unlock Challenge Mode in Garden of Witches?", "Clear Epilogue 3, keep that cleared save and choose Continue."),("Where do I enter Challenge Mode?", "Continuing the Epilogue 3-cleared save places Sil in the Challenge Mode version of her house. Prepare the build, then leave through the door."),("Why is Challenge Mode not showing?", "Most often the wrong save was loaded or Epilogue 3 has not been cleared on that save. Verify both before changing the installation.")]
challenge = '''<header class="page-hero image-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Post-Epilogue 3 endgame</p><h1>Garden of Witches Challenge Mode Guide: Unlock &amp; Enter</h1><p>Use the Epilogue 3-cleared save, prepare inside the Challenge Mode version of Sil's House, then leave through the door.</p></div><img src="../assets/media/official-challenge-mode.avif" width="800" height="450" alt="Official Garden of Witches Challenge Mode settings screen"></header><article class="article-layout"><div class="prose"><section class="direct-answer"><b>Direct answer</b><p>Challenge Mode unlocks after you clear <strong>Epilogue 3</strong>. Keep and continue that cleared save. The game loads the Challenge Mode version of Sil's House; set the available challenge options, prepare the Armory loadout, and leave through the door to begin.</p></section><section class="quick-answer"><h2>Quick answer</h2><ol><li>Clear Chapters 1–5 and Epilogues 1–3.</li><li>Return to the title flow without replacing the cleared save.</li><li>Select Continue on the Epilogue 3-cleared save.</li><li>Confirm Sil's House shows the Challenge Mode state.</li><li>Prepare the loadout and exit through the door.</li></ol></section><h2 id="requirements">Unlock requirements</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Required state</th><th>How to verify</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Story progress</td><td>Epilogue 3 cleared</td><td>The save must retain the final 1.0 story clear</td></tr><tr><td>Save selection</td><td>Continue the cleared save</td><td>Do not open an earlier or separate normal-story save</td></tr><tr><td>Entrance state</td><td>Challenge Mode Sil's House</td><td>The endgame preparation interface is available before leaving</td></tr><tr><td>Run start</td><td>Exit through the house door</td><td>The selected challenge setup applies to the new run</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="prepare">Prepare before leaving Sil's House</h2><p>Challenge Mode is the point where a coherent loadout matters more than an attractive list of bonuses. Equip Scissors whose input rhythm you can sustain under pressure, a Spell that covers its weak moment and a Special Skill with one clear job. Use the real-time DPS UI for comparisons, but read damage taken and clear consistency alongside the number.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>Broken Scissors route: confirm you can maintain contact long enough to build Sharpness.</li><li>Magic Scissors route: confirm there is enough space to cross the first charge gauge and aim.</li><li>Keep one fallback Imprint branch for runs where the preferred reward does not appear.</li><li>Read the current 1.0 tooltip for previewed Relics before depending on detailed values.</li></ul><h2 id="missing">Challenge Mode does not appear</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Check</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Continue opens normal Sil's House</td><td>Save timestamp and cleared chapter</td><td>Load the exact save that cleared Epilogue 3</td></tr><tr><td>Epilogue 3 is unavailable</td><td>Earlier chapter and Epilogue progression</td><td>Complete the remaining story route first</td></tr><tr><td>House is correct but the run does not start</td><td>Whether Sil left through the door</td><td>Finish preparation and use the house exit</td></tr><tr><td>Guide instructions mention a different unlock</td><td>Guide version</td><td>Discard Early Access instructions and use the 1.0 sequence</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="boundary">What is confirmed</h2><p class="source-note">The unlock after Epilogue 3, continued cleared save, Challenge Mode Sil's House and door exit come from Team Tapas' 1.0 release notes. Individual difficulty options and balance can change; read the current screen before committing the run.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Team Tapas official release notes</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Site evidence and media ledger</a></li></ul></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>Prepare the next run</h2><a href="../walkthrough.html">Complete the story route</a><a href="armory.html">Check the Armory</a><a href="../builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Compare two documented build paths</a><a href="controls.html">Set controls for the chosen rhythm</a></div>''' + faq_html(challenge_faq) + '''</div><aside class="toc"><b>On this page</b><a href="#requirements">Requirements</a><a href="#prepare">Build preparation</a><a href="#missing">Mode missing</a><a href="#boundary">Evidence</a></aside></article>'''
walkthrough = inject_before_faq(walkthrough, '''<h2 id="route-build">Build continuity across the route</h2><p>Do not replace a functioning loadout merely because a new item unlocks. Keep the old baseline, read the new tooltip and test one slot in the next comparable room. Chapter progress asks for reliable execution more often than a theoretical maximum assembled from unfamiliar parts.</p><p>Before each clear attempt, identify one failure from the prior run: interrupted combo, unsafe charge, missing range, weak group control or poor recovery. Change the slot that addresses that failure. After the attempt, check whether the symptom changed. This creates a useful progression record even when random rewards differ.</p><h2 id="save-discipline">Save-state discipline</h2><p>Use the most recent progressing save for Chapters and Epilogues. After Epilogue 3, preserve that cleared state and choose Continue. If the interface opens normal story Sil's House, verify the selected save before reinstalling or changing files. The official transition depends on progress state, not a secret menu combination.</p>''')
challenge = inject_before_faq(challenge, '''<h2 id="challenge-test">First Challenge Mode test</h2><p>Begin with the stable story-clear loadout rather than changing every Armory slot. Select a manageable challenge setup, run a repeatable combat window and observe where the build breaks. Use the real-time DPS display, clear time and damage taken together. Then change one component or one difficulty choice.</p><p>For Broken Scissors, measure how often the mode forces contact breaks before full Sharpness. For Magic Scissors, measure how often increased pressure interrupts charge. The answer determines whether the next change should add damage, movement, control or recovery.</p><h2 id="challenge-record">Record the endgame state</h2><ul><li>Game version and save cleared through Epilogue 3.</li><li>Visible Challenge Mode options selected before leaving the house.</li><li>Armory loadout and current tooltips.</li><li>Chapter/encounter, DPS window, clear time and damage taken.</li><li>One changed variable for the next attempt.</li></ul><p>This record turns a strong run into reusable player evidence. Without it, a high number cannot distinguish build power from an easier modifier, different encounter or lucky reward sequence.</p>''')

sources = '''<header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence and media desk</p><h1>Sources, version labels and game media</h1><p>Every mechanics claim identifies whether it comes from final 1.0 notes, an official preview or repeatable player testing.</p></header><article class="article-layout"><div class="prose"><h2>Primary sources</h2><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Team Tapas Steam news</a> — 1.0 launch notes and pre-launch examples.</li><li><a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/2530470/Garden_of_Witches/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Garden of Witches Steam page</a> — store facts, screenshots and media.</li></ul><h2>Evidence labels</h2><dl><dt>Official 1.0</dt><dd>Confirmed in the Aug 28 full-release notes.</dd><dt>Official preview</dt><dd>Published by Team Tapas before launch; detailed values may have changed.</dd><dt>Player-tested</dt><dd>Requires a named version, loadout, chapter and repeatable comparison.</dd></dl><h2>Media usage</h2><p>Game screenshots, icons, animations and key art were downloaded from official Steam or Team Tapas announcements. They remain © Team Tapas, Ltd. Files are served locally; retrieval URLs and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in <code>assets/media/source-manifest.json</code>.</p><div class="shot-grid sources-gallery"><img src="assets/media/steam-screenshot-00.jpg" width="600" height="338" loading="lazy" alt="Sil's room in Garden of Witches"><img src="assets/media/steam-screenshot-03.jpg" width="600" height="338" loading="lazy" alt="Garden of Witches boss battle"><img src="assets/media/steam-screenshot-07.jpg" width="600" height="338" loading="lazy" alt="Garden of Witches illustrated story screen"></div><h2>Correction format</h2><pre class="template">Page URL:\nClaim to correct:\nGame version shown:\nScissors / Spell / Imprint / Relic:\nChapter and difficulty:\nScreenshot or uncut clip:</pre></div><aside class="toc"><b>Last checked</b><p>29 Aug 2026</p><b>Target version</b><p>1.0 full release</p></aside></article>'''
