# Final depth pass: distinct player-use sections bring commercial pages into the
# 1,500-word editorial target and supporting guides above 900 words.
home += '''<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Player-first editorial model</p><h2>Facts, routes and unknowns stay separate.</h2></div><p>A player arrives with a symptom, not a request for a fictional encyclopedia. The site therefore starts with the build loop, weapon cadence, save state or control problem that blocks progress. It then connects the answer to official 1.0 facts and tells the player what to verify in the current tooltip.</p><p>This makes updates tractable. A balance change can alter an Imprint value without destroying the whole guide because the page separates the stable action loop from provisional details. A new player capture can fill the Singing Scissors profile without copying an unsupported number. A corrected unlock state can update one fact table and its FAQ answer.</p><p>Official media follows the same discipline. Screenshots, posters, videos and icons come from Team Tapas or Steam sources, carry descriptive alt text and live in a hashed local manifest. Each core page uses media relevant to the player task instead of sharing one generic image.</p><p>To submit a useful correction, record the page, claim, version, save progress, full loadout, chapter, difficulty and an uncut screenshot or clip. That evidence lets the editorial desk distinguish a released fact, preview example and repeatable player result.</p><div class="related-reading"><h2>Follow the complete route</h2><a href="guides/getting-started.html">First run</a><a href="guides/armory.html">Armory setup</a><a href="walkthrough.html">Story route</a><a href="guides/challenge-mode.html">Endgame</a></div></section>'''
best = inject_before_faq(best, '''<h2 id="best-record">Build record minimum</h2><p>For a reusable result, record version 1.0, the chapter and difficulty, every Armory slot, selected Imprints and Relics, and one changed component. Capture a current tooltip when a previewed effect matters. An uncut combat sample should show setup, payoff and recovery. This prevents a lucky burst, different modifier or easier room from becoming a universal claim.</p><p>The best build is therefore a verified decision process: choose the executable rhythm, assemble functional jobs, adapt to drops and compare one variable. Future balance evidence can update a component without rewriting the entire player workflow.</p>''')
broken = inject_before_faq(broken, '''<h2 id="broken-practice">Practice without ideal drops</h2><p>Run the base Broken Scissors loop before judging Hunger, Frenzy or Cat's Eye Ring. Approach, land enough real hits to observe Sharpness, leave safely and repeat. Once that motion works, add one interaction and watch whether it improves uptime or merely adds complexity.</p><p>During a failed run, classify the failure. If enemies escape, improve approach or control. If Sil takes damage while staying close, shorten the conversion window or add recovery. If Sharpness builds but the crit state finds no target, change target selection. Only a confirmed tooltip mismatch calls for changing the written mechanic.</p><p>For a reproducible report, capture the complete build-build-exit cycle rather than a single full-gauge frame. Include the current tooltips and compare one branch on the same encounter. This separates player execution from reward luck and makes the next correction concrete.</p>''')
magic = inject_before_faq(magic, '''<h2 id="magic-practice">Practice and isolate the handoff</h2><p>First use Magic Scissors without depending on Blue Chakram or a preferred Imprint. Create space, aim through more than one target, cross the confirmed threshold and release. Next add Fireball and practice the handoff only when the target state is stable. Finally add one branch and compare the same encounter.</p><p>If the base sequence works but the complete build fails, remove pieces in reverse order. This isolates whether the problem comes from branch behavior, resource timing, Spell charge or basic spacing. It also keeps an impressive preview animation from hiding a loadout the player cannot reproduce.</p><p>A useful result captures the full sequence, current tooltips, chapter, difficulty, sustained DPS, clear time and damage taken. Compare Threading and Downpour separately from Rapid Fire and Fragment. Changing both sides at once cannot show which branch caused the difference.</p>''')
weapons = inject_before_faq(weapons, '''<h2 id="weapon-evidence">Evidence checklist for a complete profile</h2><p>A full weapon profile needs the current name, tooltip, defining input, observed range in a versioned capture, unlock state and at least one repeatable combat sample. Pairing advice should explain which weak moment it solves. A ranking needs controlled comparisons rather than different chapters or modifier states.</p><p>This standard is why Singing Scissors remains explicitly incomplete here. The missing mechanic becomes a research task, not an invitation to rewrite a competitor's unsupported number. When primary or reproducible evidence arrives, the page can add its cadence, role and troubleshooting without changing the evidence model.</p><p>For any newly unlocked Scissors, preserve the Armory screen, save progress and tooltip. State only that it was available after the recorded state unless multiple captures isolate the exact condition. That phrasing prevents one player's sequence from turning into a false universal unlock rule.</p>''')
changes = inject_before_faq(changes, '''<h2 id="legacy-filter">Use this page as a legacy-guide filter</h2><p>Before applying any build recipe, check its date, menus and component names. If it requires Attribute, Synergy or Rune systems, identify the action it tried to improve and rebuild that action with current Scissors, Spells, Imprints and Relics. Route to the Weapons guide for cadence, the Armory guide for starting slots and the Build guide for verified interactions.</p><p>Keep the original page only as historical context. Current tooltips and the 1.0 release structure control the playable answer.</p>''')
armory = inject_before_faq(armory, '''<h2 id="armory-scenarios">Three Armory scenarios</h2><p><strong>New save:</strong> keep the default Scissors, learn its complete combo and choose a Spell that creates a safe opening. <strong>New unlock:</strong> change one slot and practice the defining input before comparing. <strong>Post-Epilogue 3:</strong> preserve the story-clear baseline for the first Challenge Mode test, then adapt from observed failure.</p><p>After every return, inspect permanent options before assuming a failed run produced nothing. When an expected item is absent, verify the correct save and progress state. Exact unlock conditions require direct evidence; this guide does not turn one player's timing into a universal rule.</p><h2 id="armory-ab">A/B test an unlock</h2><p>Save the old loadout, equip one new component and enter the same progression state. Perform the defining input correctly, then record sustained DPS, clear time, interruptions and damage taken. Keep the unlock only when it fixes the intended weakness without breaking the primary loop. A newly available Scissors is a different rhythm, not an automatic numerical upgrade.</p><div class="related-reading"><h2>Continue the loadout workflow</h2><a href="getting-started.html">First-run decisions</a><a href="weapons.html">Weapon profiles</a><a href="challenge-mode.html">Endgame preparation</a></div>''')
controls = inject_before_faq(controls, '''<h2 id="control-audit">Control audit after a failed room</h2><p>Separate tactical failure from input failure. If the correct action was chosen but the player could not activate it while moving, adjust the binding. If the input fired correctly but the timing was unsafe, keep the layout and practice the encounter decision. Changing both controls and loadout at once hides the cause.</p><p>For charged builds, record aim direction, charge threshold and whether movement remained available. For combo builds, record where the chain stops. For gamepad, confirm the intended device remains active after menus. These checks create a dependable setup without publishing a brittle universal key map.</p><h2 id="control-practice">One-room rehearsal</h2><p>Test the Scissors input, Spell and Special Skill together for one complete room after any binding change. The support action must remain reachable exactly when the weapon becomes unsafe. Prefer repeatable movement and activation over a theoretically faster layout that creates finger conflicts. Follow the current settings labels because platform and localization presentation can differ.</p><div class="source-list"><h3>Sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/2530470/allnews/" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Team Tapas 1.0 notes</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Site source policy</a></li></ul></div>''')
challenge = inject_before_faq(challenge, '''<h2 id="challenge-first-test">First Challenge Mode comparison</h2><p>Begin with the stable story-clear loadout rather than changing every Armory slot. Select a manageable challenge setup, run a repeatable combat window and observe where the build breaks. Use the real-time DPS display, clear time and damage taken together, then change one component or one difficulty choice.</p><p>For Broken Scissors, measure how often added pressure forces contact breaks before full Sharpness. For Magic Scissors, measure interrupted charges and missed release lines. The result tells you whether the next reward should add damage, movement, control or recovery.</p><h2 id="challenge-evidence">Endgame record</h2><p>Record version, Epilogue 3-cleared save, visible challenge options, Armory loadout, tooltips, encounter and one changed variable. This turns a strong run into reusable evidence instead of confusing modifier choice or reward luck with build strength.</p>''')
home += '''<section class="section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Answer-engine summary</p><h2>The stable 1.0 facts</h2><p>Garden of Witches version 1.0 launched on 28 August 2026. Its build system uses Scissors, Spells, Imprints and Relics rather than the removed Attribute, Synergy and Rune systems. Official material names five Scissors. Story progress covers five main chapters and three Epilogues. Clearing Epilogue 3 unlocks Challenge Mode on the continued cleared save.</p><p>The site treats specific build routes as documented interactions rather than universal tier rankings. Broken Scissors centers on Sharpness from repeated hits. Magic Scissors centers on charged piercing projectiles and pairs with Fireball in an official example. Current tooltips decide detailed effects whenever a pre-launch preview and the installed release differ.</p></div><aside class="note"><b>Fast source check</b><p>Official Team Tapas news establishes systems and progression. The Steam store establishes platform and official media. Player conclusions require a versioned, repeatable capture.</p></aside></section>'''
broken = inject_before_faq(broken, '''<h2 id="broken-summary">When to choose this build</h2><p>Choose Broken Scissors when the player can read close-range openings, reconnect after movement and spend a full Sharpness state on a target that remains in reach. Avoid presenting it as best when the current challenge repeatedly forces long disengagement or the player cannot see incoming attacks while maintaining contact.</p><p>The route remains valid without every previewed reward because its stable question is functional: can the loadout build, preserve and convert Sharpness safely? Use Hunger, Frenzy and Cat's Eye Ring only after the current tooltip confirms that they solve one of those jobs.</p>''')
magic = inject_before_faq(magic, '''<h2 id="magic-summary">When to choose this build</h2><p>Choose Magic Scissors when the player can establish space, aim along a useful line and release a charge before pressure closes the gap. Fireball becomes a practical partner when the same spacing supports its charge and the current Blue Chakram tooltip confirms the weapon-to-Spell bridge.</p><p>A ranged route is not automatically safer. Time spent charging creates exposure, missed lanes waste piercing and delayed Fireballs can lose the target. Judge the build by repeatable complete cycles, not by the largest isolated projectile.</p>''')
weapons = inject_before_faq(weapons, '''<h2 id="weapon-summary">The selection rule</h2><p>Use the default or Giant Scissors family when finishing a full combo feels reliable. Use Magic Scissors when aim and charge timing are reliable. Use Broken Scissors when repeated close contact is reliable. For Singing Scissors, inspect the live tooltip before making any role claim.</p><p>The best weapon is the one whose defining condition survives the player's real chapter pressure. Compare with the same supporting loadout and encounter so a Spell, random reward or difficulty change does not decide the result.</p>''')
changes = inject_before_faq(changes, '''<p class="source-note">This page targets the 28 August 2026 full release. Recheck official announcements and the current in-game tooltip after any later balance update.</p>''')
