def replace_home_section(body, marker, replacement):
    marker_at = body.index(marker)
    start = body.rfind("<section", 0, marker_at)
    end = body.index("</section>", marker_at) + len("</section>")
    return body[:start] + replacement + body[end:]


# Reorder the long homepage around first-session jobs instead of editorial process.
home = replace_home_section(home, "Editorial method", '''<section class="section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Before the first room</p><h2>Make four actions feel separate.</h2><p>Move, aim, attack and dash in a low-pressure space before committing to a route. Keep Keyboard &amp; Mouse when free aim feels natural. Try Keyboard-Only or Gamepad when the pointer competes with movement.</p><p>Stay with the default Scissors long enough to recognize its full combo and its unsafe moment. Your supporting Spell or Special Skill should create space for that moment, not start a second unrelated plan.</p><a class="text-link" href="guides/getting-started.html">Follow the complete first-run checklist →</a></div><aside class="note"><b>60-second readiness check</b><ul><li>Move away while aiming at a target</li><li>Finish one combo only in a safe opening</li><li>Dash without losing the target</li><li>Name the reward before entering a door</li></ul></aside></section>''')

home = replace_home_section(home, "How to use this wiki", '''<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">First-session answers</p><h2>Match the symptom to one next action.</h2></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>What you see</th><th>Read this</th><th>Do this next</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>You do not know what to press or practice</td><td><a href="guides/getting-started.html">Beginner Guide</a></td><td>Complete the four-action readiness check</td></tr><tr><td>A door reward makes no sense</td><td><a href="guides/rooms-and-map.html">Rooms &amp; Map</a></td><td>Choose recovery first when health limits the run</td></tr><tr><td>Progress or upgrades appear to be gone</td><td><a href="guides/upgrades-reset.html">Upgrade Reset Guide</a></td><td>Identify run-only progress versus Tapestry progress</td></tr><tr><td>Attacks point the wrong way</td><td><a href="guides/controls.html">Controls</a></td><td>Test one complete room with a different scheme</td></tr><tr><td>Damage improves but the run still fails</td><td><a href="builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Build Planner</a></td><td>Measure clear time and damage taken, not peak DPS</td></tr><tr><td>The next story step is unclear</td><td><a href="walkthrough.html">Walkthrough</a></td><td>Verify the latest clear on the current save</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Do not change controls, weapon and several rewards at the same time. One deliberate change makes the next result understandable.</p></section>''')

home = replace_home_section(home, "Player-first editorial model", '''<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Your first 20 minutes</p><h2>Learn one loop before chasing a perfect build.</h2></div><div class="progress-map"><span><b>1. Rehearse</b><br>Move, aim, combo and dash</span><span><b>2. Read</b><br>Check the next reward icon</span><span><b>3. Commit</b><br>Support one damage action</span><span><b>4. Preserve</b><br>Take recovery when health is the bottleneck</span><span><b>5. Review</b><br>Return home after the run</span><strong>6. Change one thing<br>Then compare again</strong></div><p>A failed room is useful when it tells you whether the problem was input, route choice, damage uptime or survival. Write down that one failure before changing the loadout. If the next run improves the same symptom, keep the change. If not, restore the baseline.</p><p>New unlocks are choices, not automatic upgrades. Practice a new Scissors until you can perform its defining combo, charge or resource loop before comparing it with the default weapon.</p><div class="related-reading"><h2>Keep learning in order</h2><a href="guides/getting-started.html">First-run guide</a><a href="guides/rooms-and-map.html">Room and map choices</a><a href="guides/armory.html">Armory setup</a><a href="guides/weapons.html">Weapon comparison</a></div></section>''')

home = replace_home_section(home, "Answer-engine summary", '''<section class="section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Progress explained</p><h2>Run power and permanent progress are different.</h2><p>Imprints, Relics and other rewards assembled inside a run are temporary. Returning to Sil's House starts the next attempt without that exact stack. Level-based upgrades selected through the house progression system are permanent and should not silently disappear from the same save.</p><p>Version 1.0 launched with reports of permanent upgrade levels resetting after chapter or save transitions. The developer treated those reports as a bug investigation. If that is what happened, stop grinding, preserve the save and record before/after screens.</p><a class="text-link" href="guides/upgrades-reset.html">Diagnose an upgrade reset →</a></div><aside class="note"><b>Fast distinction</b><p><strong>Expected:</strong> the in-run build starts over.</p><p><strong>Not expected:</strong> spent permanent nodes or character level vanish from the same save.</p></aside></section>''')

