getting_started = inject_before_faq(getting_started, '''<h2 id="timeline">Your first run, moment by moment</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Moment</th><th>Best beginner action</th><th>Ready to continue when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Before leaving Sil's House</td><td>Keep the default Scissors and a simple support action</td><td>You can explain what each equipped input does</td></tr><tr><td>Opening room</td><td>Practice movement, aim, combo and dash separately</td><td>You can leave danger without losing your target</td></tr><tr><td>At a door</td><td>Read the visible reward before entering</td><td>The choice improves the current loop or protects health</td></tr><tr><td>Before a major fight</td><td>Keep movement available and stop experimenting</td><td>You know the safe attack window and an exit path</td></tr><tr><td>After defeat or a clear</td><td>Return home, inspect progress and change one slot</td><td>The next attempt has one stated purpose</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="priority">Reward priority for a beginner</h2><ol><li><strong>Health is the limit:</strong> if another hit can end the run, recovery is worth more than a conditional damage reward.</li><li><strong>Execution comes next:</strong> if the combo or charge is constantly interrupted, take movement, control or reach that lets the action happen.</li><li><strong>Then reinforce damage:</strong> prefer a reward whose trigger already occurs in the current loadout.</li><li><strong>Skip fake synergy:</strong> a rare Relic is not useful when the other half of its condition is missing.</li><li><strong>Read current wording:</strong> the installed tooltip wins over an Early Access guide or launch preview value.</li></ol><h2 id="after-run">After the run: expected reset or real problem?</h2><div class="table-wrap troubleshooting"><table><thead><tr><th>What changed</th><th>Normal?</th><th>Next step</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Imprints, Relics and run rewards are gone</td><td>Yes, these form the temporary run build</td><td>Use the result to plan the next route</td></tr><tr><td>A different room order appears</td><td>Yes, placement and clear rewards can vary</td><td>Read the map again instead of memorizing a route</td></tr><tr><td>Spent permanent upgrade nodes or level disappear</td><td>No, current 1.0 reports treat this as a save/progression bug</td><td>Preserve the save and follow the upgrade reset checklist</td></tr><tr><td>A new Scissors feels weaker</td><td>Possible; an unlock is a new rhythm, not a straight upgrade</td><td>Practice its defining input before comparing</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="related-reading"><h2>New-player problem guides</h2><a href="rooms-and-map.html">Rooms, map and route choices</a><a href="upgrades-reset.html">Upgrade reset diagnosis</a><a href="controls.html">Control setup</a><a href="../builds/garden-of-witches-best-build.html">Build after the basics</a></div>''')
